  1309 Aug 17 13:18 story-attempt1.output\\n-rw-r--r--  1 root root   1553 Aug 17 13:18 summary.json\\n-rw-r--r--  1 root root  40489 Aug 17 13:18 test-attempt1.log\\n-rw-r--r--  1 root root   2817 Aug 17 13:18 test-attempt1.output\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"user\", \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_01XBS4F2wLtLSAxP4Z2BfmVZ\", \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n17\t{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T13:19:05Z\", \"agent\": \"claude-edits\", \"seq\": 17, \"kind\": \"tool_result\", \"text\": \"{\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"finished\\\",\\n  \\\"reason\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"dispatches\\\": 12,\\n  \\\"attempts\\\": {\\n    \\\"story\\\": 1,\\n    \\\"design\\\": 1,\\n    \\\"build\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"review\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"test\\\": 1\\n  },\\n  \\\"stages\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"stage\\\": \\\"story\\\",\\n      \\\"ok\\\": true,\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"stage\\\": \\\"design\\\",\\n      \\\"ok\\\": true,\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"stage\\\": \\\"build/frontend\\\",\\n      \\\"ok\\\": true,\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"stage\\\": \\\"build/backend\\\",\\n      \\\"ok\\\": true,\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"stage\\\": \\\"review\\\",\\n      \\\"ok\\\": true,\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"stage\\\": \\\"build/frontend\\\",\\n      \\\"ok\\\": true,\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"stage\\\": \\\"build/backend\\\",\\n      \\\"ok\\\": true,\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"stage\\\": \\\"review\\\",\\n      \\\"ok\\\": true,\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"stage\\\": \\\"build/frontend\\\",\\n      \\\"ok\\\": true,\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"stage\\\": \\\"build/backend\\\",\\n      \\\"ok\\\": true,\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"stage\\\": \\\"review\\\",\\n      \\\"ok\\\": true,\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"approve-with-followups\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"stage\\\": \\\"test\\\",\\n      \\\"ok\\\": true,\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"pass\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"seconds\\\": 1438.5,\\n  \\\"task\\\": \\\"Taiga #13: Let me undo deleting a task.\\\\n\\\\nDeleting is immediate and there is no way back, which makes me hesitant to use it. After deleting a task, give me a brief chance to undo it and get the task back exactly as it was, including whether it was completed.\\\",\\n  \\\"workdir\\\": \\\"/home/dev/projects/test-project\\\"\\n}\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"user\", \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_01CXMnpuGFqSFq6pnHgFpLmH\", \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n18\t{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T13:19:07Z\", \"agent\": \"claude-edits\", \"seq\": 18, \"kind\": \"status\", \"text\": \"\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"system\", \"subtype\": \"thinking_tokens\", \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n19\t{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T13:19:08Z\", \"agent\": \"claude-edits\", \"seq\": 19, \"kind\": \"status\", \"text\": \"\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"system\", \"subtype\": \"thinking_tokens\", \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n20\t{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T13:19:08Z\", \"agent\": \"claude-edits\", \"seq\": 20, \"kind\": \"status\", \"text\": \"\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"assistant\", \"block_type\": \"thinking\", \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n21\t{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T13:19:09Z\", \"agent\": \"claude-edits\", \"seq\": 21, \"kind\": \"tool_use\", \"text\": \"Bash\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"assistant\", \"block_type\": \"tool_use\", \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_01EdVMvjFASG1wXLo8G5v2an\", \"input\": {\"command\": \"ls -la /home/dev/projects/ai-dev-switchboard/docs/agent-rework/round-09-logs/retro/ 2>/dev/null; echo \\\"---\\\"; cat /home/dev/projects/ai-dev-switchboard/docs/agent-rework/round-09-logs/review-attempt1.output\"}, \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n22\t{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T13:19:09Z\", \"agent\": \"claude-edits\", \"seq\": 22, \"kind\": \"tool_result\", \"text\": \"total 20\\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Aug 17 13:19 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 root root 4096 Aug 17 13:18 ..\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 8318 Aug 17 13:19 retrospective-attempt1.log\\n---\\n## Review summary\\n\\n**Will block**\\n\\n- **`frontend/src/App.jsx:125` (Alan Heitkotter \\u2014 failure paths) / `frontend/src/components/UndoToast.jsx:6`** \\u2014 `pendingDeleteIds` is never reconciled against `tasks`, so when a pending-delete task disappears from `tasks` via some *other* refresh, the toast crashes. Concrete repro: delete a completed task (leaves it pending-undo, still in `tasks`), then click \\\"Clear completed\\\" before the 5s window elapses. That bulk-deletes the (done) task server-side and refreshes `tasks`, which no longer contains it \\u2014 but `pendingDeleteIds` still does. `tasks.find(...)` returns `undefined`, and `UndoToast.jsx:6`'s `key={task.id}` throws on it. No error boundary exists, so this is a full UI crash, not a cosmetic glitch. This is exactly the race the spec's own AC6 anticipates (Clear Completed vs. a pending delete) \\u2014 the code handles the async 404 from that race but not this synchronous state-desync from it.\\n\\n**Will comment**\\n\\n- **`frontend/src/App.jsx:19` (Christopher Zipp \\u2014 reuse/data modelling)** \\u2014 `pendingDeleteIds` (state) and `pendingDeleteTimers.current` (ref Map) track the identical key set in two places, always mutated together. Not a bug today, but it's the kind of duplicate source of truth that produced the blocker above; collapsing to one `Map<id, timerHandle>` (deriving the id list from its keys) removes a spot a future edit has to remember to touch twice.\\n\\n**Worth considering**\\n\\n- None.\\n\\nEverything else checks out: the frontend-only design decision is sound and well-justified, all six acceptance criteria are otherwise met (immediate hide, exact-state restore since nothing is mutated, 5s auto-delete, done-state preserved, independent multi-undo via array+Map, 404 swallowed on the *timer* path), `TaskList.jsx`/`api.js`/backend correctly left untouched, and the CSS/a11y choices match the design doc and existing `.error`/`TaskCounts` conventions.\\n\\nVERDICT: changes-requested\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"user\", \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_01EdVMvjFASG1wXLo8G5v2an\", \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n23\t{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T13:19:09Z\", \"agent\": \"claude-edits\", \"seq\": 23, \"kind\": \"tool_use\", \"text\": \"Bash\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"assistant\", \"block_type\": \"tool_use\", \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_01BaSUWVr42syRjDSuQLYVVW\", \"input\": {\"command\": \"cat /home/dev/projects/ai-dev-switchboard/docs/agent-rework/round-09-logs/review-attempt2.output\"}, \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n24\t{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T13:19:09Z\", \"agent\": \"claude-edits\", \"seq\": 24, \"kind\": \"tool_result\", \"text\": \"## Review: Taiga #13 \\u2014 Let me undo deleting a task (attempt 2)\\n\\nVerified against `docs/spec.md`'s 6 ACs and `docs/design.md`. Confirmed the round-1 crash (`UndoToast.jsx:6` on `Clear completed` racing a pending delete) is genuinely fixed \\u2014 `pending={tasks.filter((t) => pendingDeletes.has(t.id))}` naturally excludes a task once it drops out of `tasks`, so no `undefined` reaches the map. `npm run build` passes. I could not spin up a live browser repro (dev server launch needs approval this headless session doesn't have \\u2014 same gap noted in the developer's handoff for `npm run lint`), so the flicker finding below is a traced-through-code finding, not a live repro; the trace is based on standard JS/React execution order and I'm confident in it, but flagging the verification gap per the \\\"report honestly\\\" convention.\\n\\n## Will block\\n\\n**`frontend/src/App.jsx:76-93`** (Alan Heitkotter \\u2014 failure paths / ordering of effects). `deferDelete`'s timer callback removes the id from `pendingDeletes` **before** awaiting `api.deleteTask(id)`:\\n\\n```js\\nconst timer = setTimeout(async () => {\\n  setPendingDeletes((prev) => { ... next.delete(id); return next })  // \\u2190 commits first\\n  try {\\n    await api.deleteTask(id)   // \\u2190 network round trip happens after\\n    await refresh()\\n  } ...\\n```\\n\\nSince `activeTasks` is computed as `tasks.filter((t) => !pendingDeletes.has(t.id))` (App.jsx:39), the moment this state update commits, the task is back in `activeTasks` \\u2014 it reappears in the list, counts, and filters \\u2014 because `tasks` itself hasn't been touched yet. Only once `refresh()` resolves (a real network round trip later) does the task disappear again. This isn't a rare race: it's the **default path**, every time a delete is left to expire naturally (the common case \\u2014 no undo clicked). The user sees: toast disappears \\u2192 task flashes back into the list, fully interactive (Edit/Done/Delete all live again) \\u2192 task vanishes a moment later with no toast, no warning. That directly undermines AC3 (\\\"the DELETE request is sent... and the notice disappears on its own\\\") and the feature's whole premise of a clean, predictable deletion.\\n\\n**Fix:** don't release the `pendingDeletes` entry until the delete attempt (success or the swallowed 404) is settled \\u2014 move the `setPendingDeletes` removal into a `finally` after the `try`/`catch`, not before it:\\n\\n```js\\nconst timer = setTimeout(async () => {\\n  try {\\n    await api.deleteTask(id)\\n    await refresh()\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    if (e.message !== 'no such task') setError(e.message)\\n  } finally {\\n    setPendingDeletes((prev) => { const next = new Map(prev); next.delete(id); return next })\\n  }\\n}, UNDO_WINDOW_MS)\\n```\\n\\n## Will comment\\n\\n**`frontend/src/App.jsx:134`** (Eric Goto \\u2014 list/collection ordering). `docs/design.md:41` and `:80` explicitly specify \\\"oldest pending-delete first\\\" stacking, and the original design's data shape (`pendingDeleteIds.map(...)`) preserved deletion order. The round-2 fix switched to `tasks.filter((t) => pendingDeletes.has(t.id))`, which orders by `tasks`' own order (task creation/list order), not deletion order. Delete two tasks out of list order and the toast stack no longer matches \\\"oldest deleted on top\\\" as documented. Not a crash, but a documented design commitment that's silently not met.\\n\\n**Fix:** iterate `pendingDeletes`' own key order (a `Map` preserves insertion order) and guard against a since-vanished task, keeping both the crash fix and the deletion-order guarantee:\\n```js\\npending={[...pendingDeletes.keys()].map((id) => tasks.find((t) => t.id === id)).filter(Boolean)}\\n```\\n\\n## Worth considering\\n\\n**`frontend/src/App.jsx:96-103`** (Alan Heitkotter \\u2014 purity of state updaters). `cancelPendingDelete`'s `setPendingDeletes` updater calls `clearTimeout(prev.get(id))` as a side effect inside the updater function. React (especially under `StrictMode`, which `main.jsx:6` enables) may invoke updaters more than once to surface impurities; here it's harmless since `clearTimeout` on an already-cleared/`undefined` handle is a no-op, but it's worth moving the `clearTimeout` call outside the updater (read `pendingDeletes.get(id)` from render scope, or use a ref) if this pattern gets reused elsewhere.\\n\\nVERDICT: changes-requested\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"user\", \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_01BaSUWVr42syRjDSuQLYVVW\", \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n25\t{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T13:19:11Z\", \"agent\": \"claude-edits\", \"seq\": 25, \"kind\": \"status\", \"text\": \"\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"system\", \"subtype\": \"thinking_tokens\", \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n26\t{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T13:19:13Z\", \"agent\": \"claude-edits\", \"seq\": 26, \"kind\": \"status\", \"text\": \"\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"system\", \"subtype\": \"thinking_tokens\", \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n27\t{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T13:19:14Z\", \"agent\": \"claude-edits\", \"seq\": 27, \"kind\": \"status\", \"text\": \"\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"system\", \"subtype\": \"thinking_tokens\", \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n28\t{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T13:19:15Z\", \"agent\": \"claude-edits\", \"seq\": 28, \"kind\": \"status\", \"text\": \"\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"system\", \"subtype\": \"thinking_tokens\", \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n29\t{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T13:19:15Z\", \"agent\": \"claude-edits\", \"seq\": 29, \"kind\": \"status\", \"text\": \"\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"assistant\", \"block_type\": \"thinking\", \"session_id\": \"bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3\"}}\n30\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01MMueFcBYyTgYeJ3awQx8HK", "session_id": "bb2c07c1-ebce-406f-bea6-1d2e18b5d6c3"}}
